# Node seats (h0, guests, web-default): only what a seat on a node needs.
# The desktop's forwarding policy is not restated; ssh's defaults already
# forward nothing.

# h0's herdr-core drives h3 as the unprivileged seat, same alias as the
# desktop's (`hc machine add h3-sl0p` there names it `h3-sl0p`). By plain name:
# h3 is on h0's LAN but not in h0's tailnet view. Deliberately NO h3-devops
# here — anything running as sl0p on h0 could use it, and devops has
# passwordless sudo; that alias lives only on the desktops.
#
# IdentitiesOnly: the seat reaches h3 as ITSELF. Without it, a session that
# arrived with a forwarded agent offers the operator's keys first and lands on
# h3 as the operator (ADR-0048: a forwarded principal is a session, never the
# seat). The file is the seat's own key, whichever seat reads this.
Host h3-sl0p
  HostName h3
  User sl0p
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
  IdentitiesOnly yes

# The four WordPress sites' live host (web-default, Hetzner), the same alias
# as tag-desktop's. By tailnet ADDRESS, not name: h0 runs with accept-dns off,
# so web-default.taild36b8.ts.net does not resolve there. The address is stable
# for as long as web-default is not re-enrolled.
Host wp-live
  HostName 100.100.20.87
  User devops
